                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_214\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix commit reverts fiat/equivalent-value amount formatting in\nTransfersTableAdapter.java back to using `Smartcoins.getFiatSymbol()` +\n`String.format(\"~ %s %.2f\", ...)`, and removes the `Locale` parameter that\nhad been added to the `TransfersTableAdapter` constructor.\n\ncandidate_214 is the commit that introduced the exact code being reverted.\nIn candidate_214:\n1. In TransfersTableAdapter.java, the working code\n   `String fiatSymbol = Smartcoins.getFiatSymbol(smartcoinAmount.getAsset());\n    String eqValue = String.format(\"~ %s %.2f\", fiatSymbol, Util.fromBase(smartcoinAmount));`\n   was commented out and replaced with:\n   `final Currency currency = Currency.getInstance(smartcoinAmount.getAsset().getSymbol());\n    NumberFormat currencyFormatter = Helper.newCurrencyFormat(getContext(), currency, locale);\n    String eqValue = currencyFormatter.format(Util.fromBase(smartcoinAmount));`\n   `Currency.getInstance()` requires a valid ISO 4217 currency code, but\n   `smartcoinAmount.getAsset().getSymbol()` returns a BitShares smartcoin\n   symbol (e.g. \"BITUSD\"/\"USD\"-like custom symbols), which is not guaranteed\n   to be a valid `Currency` code, causing this new code path to throw/crash\n   or otherwise misbehave \u2014 the bug being fixed.\n2. candidate_214 also changed the `TransfersTableAdapter` constructor to\n   accept an extra `Locale locale` parameter and updated the single call\n   site in `BalancesFragment.java` (`new TransfersTableAdapter(getContext(),\n   locale, account, ...)`) accordingly.\n\nThe fix commit's diff is a near line-for-line inverse of candidate_214's\nchange to these same two files, including matching (reversed) git blob\nhashes for TransfersTableAdapter.java (b9cad9f -> 134eb82 in candidate_214,\n134eb82 -> b9cad9f in the fix) and BalancesFragment.java, confirming the fix\nis a direct revert of the change introduced in candidate_214.\n"
